        "original_id": "c9ba570e-75d3-52b0-928a-832bdd08e161",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tony Hendra, Stephen Hawking, Lucy Hawking, John Cleese, Graham Chapman, Tim Brooke-Taylor\n- Organizations: St Albans School, Cambridge University, Cambridge University Footlights, Centre for Theoretical Cosmology, University of Cambridge\n- Products: National Lampoon The Iron On Book, George and the Big Bang\n- Roles: satirist, actor, writer, theoretical physicist, cosmologist, author, Director of Research\n\nFacts:\n- Tony Hendra was born on 10 July 1941 and is an English satirist, actor, and writer who worked mostly in the United States.\n- Stephen Hawking was born on 8 January 1942 and was an English theoretical physicist, cosmologist, author, and Director of Research at the Centre for Theoretical Cosmology within the University of Cambridge.\n- Tony Hendra attended St Albans School, where he was a classmate of Stephen Hawking.\n- In 1962, Tony Hendra was a member of the Cambridge University Footlights revue alongside John Cleese, Graham Chapman, and Tim Brooke-Taylor.\n- Tony Hendra studied at Cambridge University.\n- Tony Hendra edited National Lampoon The Iron On Book.\n- George and the Big Bang is a 2011 children's book written by Stephen Hawking and Lucy Hawking.",
